{"status":"ready","content":"<think>\r\n10x² + 260x/√3 - 1050 = 10(x² + 26x/√3 - 105)\r\n\r\nFind roots: x = [-26/√3 ± √(676/3 + 420)]/2 = [-26/√3 ± √(676/3 + 1260/3)]/2 = [-26/√3 ± √(1936/3)]/2 = [-26/√3 ± 44/√3]/2\r\n\r\nRoots: (18/√3)/2 = 9/√3 = 3√3, and (-70/√3)/2 = -35/√3\r\n\r\nSo 10(x - 3√3)(x + 35/√3)\r\n\r\nCheck: 35/√3 = 35√3/3. Hmm, let me verify.\r\n\r\nx² + (26/√3)x - 105 = (x - 3√3)(x + 35/√3)\r\n= x² + (35/√3 - 3√3)x - 3√3·35/√3\r\n= x² + (35/√3 - 9/√3)x - 105\r\n= x² + 26/√3 x - 105 ✓\r\n</think>\r\n\r\n$$\\boxed{10\\left(x-3\\sqrt{3}\\right)\\left(x+\\dfrac{35}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)}$$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4-7/livebench-003-math.txt","size":608,"mtime":1779367547}